Scenario 01: EC2 instance unreachable (security group blocks traffic)

- Services: EC2, VPC (security groups, route tables, network ACLs)
- Difficulty: Beginner
- Fault injected: The security group has no inbound rule for HTTP

Symptom

> Ticket: "My web server on EC2 is running, but I can't open the site. The browser keeps loading and then times out. Nothing has changed on the server."

Lab setup

Terraform builds:

- One VPC with a public subnet, an internet gateway, and a route to the internet
- One EC2 instance (smallest practical instance type) running a simple web server, started through user data
- One security group attached to the instance
- A `broken` variable: when `true`, the security group has no inbound HTTP rule

